  "body": [
    "Sustainable consumption and production has become the expectation rather than the exception. Fairtrade offers solutions for companies and producers to put fairness at the heart of their operations.",
    "More than two million farmers and workers are active in Fairtrade, creating a wide range of goods that meet the growing demand for sustainably sourced products.",
    "Recognition Recognition Consumers know and trust Fairtrade – We're the most widely recognized ethical label in the world, with about seven in ten consumers saying the mark has a positive impact on their perception of brands. Find out more",
    "Sourcing models that meet your needs Sourcing models that meet your needs Fairtrade offers different approaches that enable companies to make their supply chains sustainable and transparent.",
    "Stable business relationships with suppliers Stable business relationships with suppliers Fairtrade fosters long-term trading partnerships and empowers producers through training and support to increase quality and responsiveness to market trends.",
    "A certification and assurance system you can trust A certification and assurance system you can trust Fairtrade’s certification system is rigorous, independent and aligned with best-in-class practice, involving regular on-site visits by trained auditors. Our assurance scheme is compliant with ISEAL’s Assurance Code, an international code for sustainability standards.",
    "Solutions on living incomes and wages Solutions on living incomes and wages Fairtrade provides tools for companies to contribute to improved livelihoods in their supply chains.",
    "Expertise to support your company's due diligence Expertise to support your company's due diligence Whether you’re a business taking your first steps on your human rights and environmental due diligence the (HREDD) journey, or looking for more in-depth risk assessments and action plans, Fairtrade is your partner.",
    "Producers are at the heart of Fairtrade. Investing in a Fairtrade certification can give your producer organisation greater economic stability and help you to become more sustainable.",
    "Less volatile prices Less volatile prices There is a Fairtrade Minimum Price for most certifiable products. It provides producers with a safety net against falling market prices for their sold produce and allows for long-term planning.",
    "Additional Premium Additional Premium With the Fairtrade Premium producers can improve the quality of their lives, communities, and businesses. It is an additional amount of money paid on top of the agreed Fairtrade price for sold certified goods, which producers decide democratically how to use. The Fairtrade Premium is often invested in education, healthcare, and farm improvements to increase income.",
    "Have your say Have your say Fairtrade certified farmers and workers co-own and manage Fairtrade International – through elected delegates participating in the board of directors, key committees, and consultation processes, producers can influence Fairtrade’s strategy, standards, prices and premiums.",
    "Strong organizations Strong organizations With Fairtrade, small-scale farmer groups have a democratic structure and transparent administration. In plantations and hired labour settings, workers form a committee that decides on the use of the Fairtrade Premium. Fairtrade offers support to achieve this and strengthens producer organisations in the process.",
    "Market opportunities Market opportunities Fairtrade is the most recognised ethical label in the world. Fairtrade’s global network of marketing organisations can extend your reach to connect with businesses seeking sustainably sourced products under a label they trust.",
    "Power of community Power of community Your organization can join one of the three regional Fairtrade Producer Networks which provide support, training and representation for producers in the global Fairtrade system. They represent small-scale producers, workers, and other producer stakeholders. Please visit their websites for further information."
  ],
